{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795379870,"nonce":"vHwUCEcDYobfWVh8MEkOY9GCu14=","title":"Motion text draws above dropdowns and toasts","message":"Reported in the cn_demo window: with the calendar's year select open, the day numbers draw on top of the year list; toasts show page text through them the same way.\n\nCause. Text, SVGs and images inside a motion subtree (bound content, scroll-row content, and overlay roots) are collected into the motion pools, which the frame draws once, after the whole dynamic batch. The dynamic batch also holds the overlays: the select's list is in its foreground primitives, the toasts are in its ordinary primitives on a higher paint layer (z 3 against the page's 0). So every motion label below an overlay was drawn above it. Reproduced headless with `cn_demo_costs` (`COSTS_CALENDAR=1 COSTS_CALENDAR_DROPDOWN=0 COSTS_CALENDAR_SNAP=\u003cprefix\u003e` and `COSTS_CALENDAR_TOAST=1`); the fast frame and the full paint agree, so it is not a cache defect. Present at a19f0b84 and 96cbd5d0; the probe scenario does not build before 196d74c0. The order is older (motion pools after the dynamic batch since the context split); the calendar became bound content more recently, which put its text in the late pool.\n\nChecked by skipping passes: without the motion text pass all calendar labels vanish and the year list's text stays; without the dynamic batch the calendar card, the list and its text vanish; without the batch's foreground only the list vanishes.\n\nFix: the dynamic batch is drawn by paint layer, each run of primitives on one z followed by the motion content of that z (`GpuRenderer::overlay_divides_at`, `render_overlay_part`), then the batch's foreground, then the foreground motion content. A batch that does not divide at its layer boundaries (a boundary inside a group or a path run, a named sample, background glass, unordered groups) is drawn whole with all non-foreground motion content after it, as before for that case.","files":null}]}